<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>POPULATION PROJECTION_q2</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Given the following female population of Trindad in \(1960\) and \(1975\), answer the questions that follow. </p>
<p>
<table border="solid">
  <tr>
    <th width="15%", style="text-align:center">Age</th>
    <th width="15%", style="text-align:center">\(1960\)</th>
    <th width="15%", style="text-align:center">\(1975\)</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
  <td style="text-align:center">\(0-14\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@ageset_1a@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@ageset_1b@}\)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(15-29\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@ageset_2a@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@ageset_2b@}\)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(30-44\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@ageset_3a@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@ageset_3b@}\)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(45-59\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@ageset_4a@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@ageset_4b@}\)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(60+\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@ageset_5a@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\({@ageset_5b@}\)</td>
  </tr>
</table>
</p>

<hr>

<p>During the period 1960-1975, the live births were distributed as follows;</p>
<p>\(15-29 : {@births_1@}\)</p>
<p>\(30-44 : {@births_2@}\)</p>
<p>Find probability of a baby born surviving to time \(t+15\) denoted as \(\textbf{p}_{b}\)</p>
<p>\(\textbf{p}_{b}=\) [[input:ans1]] correct to \(3\) dp [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<hr>

<p>Given the population projection table for \(1990\) as shown below find the value of \(f_1-f_3\) where  \(\text{f}\) is the Average number of women in the fertility group  \(15-29\),\(30-44\) and the growth rate,determine the projection fertility rate \(f1,f2  \text{and}  f3\) </p>
<br>
<p>\(\begin{bmatrix}
f1 &f2  & f3 & 0 & 0\\ 
{@p_1_rate@} & 0 & 0 & 0 &0 \\ 
0 & {@p_2_rate@} & 0 &0  &0 \\ 
 0& 0 & {@p_3_rate@} & 0 & 0\\ 
0 & 0 &0  & {@p_4_rate@} & {@p_5_rate@}
\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}
v(1,t)\\ 
v(2,t)\\ 
v(3,t)\\ 
v(4,t)\\ 
v(5,t)
\end{bmatrix}\)</p>
<p>growth rate of \(p4=p5\)</p>
<p>Note: Leave your answer correct to \(3\) dp</p>
<p>\(\text{f}_1=\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>\(\text{f}_2=\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]][[feedback:prt3]]</p>
<p>\(\text{f}_3=\) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]][[feedback:prt4]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>

<table border="solid" style="width: 100%;">
  <tr>
    <th width="25%" style="text-align:center">Age</th>
    <th width="25%" style="text-align:center">\(1960\)</th>
    <th width="25%" style="text-align:center">\(1975\)</th>
    <th width="25%" style="text-align:center">Projection \(1990\)</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(0-14\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(V(1,t)={@ageset_1a@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(V(1,t+15)={@ageset_1b@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(V(1,t)→P1\)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(15-29\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(V(2,t)={@ageset_2a@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(V(2,t+15)={@ageset_2b@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(V(2,t)→P2\)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(30-44\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(V(3,t)={@ageset_3a@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(V(3,t+15)={@ageset_3b@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(V(3,t)→P3\)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(45-59\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(V(4,t)={@ageset_4a@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(V(4,t+15)={@ageset_4b@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(V(4,t)→P4\)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(60+\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(V(5,t)={@ageset_5a@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(V(5,t+15)={@ageset_5b@}\)</td>
    <td style="text-align:center">\(V(5,t)→P5\)</td>
  </tr>
</table>
</p>
<hr>
<p>To find the probability that a child born survives,</p>
<p>\(\textbf{p}_{b}=\displaystyle \frac{V(1,t+15)}{\text{total lives births}}=\displaystyle \frac{{@ageset_1b@}}{{@births_1+births_2@}}={@p_b@}\)</p>
<p>To find growth rates, \(\text{p}_1-\text{p}_5\)where \(\text{p}_4=\text{p}_5\) we proceed as follows</p>
<p>\(\text{p}_1=\displaystyle \frac{V(2,t+15)}{V(1,t)}\) where \(15\) is the the years for which you have data.</p>
<p>\(=\displaystyle \frac{{@ageset_2b@}}{{@ageset_1a@}}={@p_1_rate@}\)</p>
<br>
<p>\(\text{p}_2=\displaystyle \frac{V(3,t+15)}{V(2,t)}=\displaystyle \frac{{@ageset_3b@}}{{@ageset_2a@}}={@p_2_rate@},   \text{p}_3=\displaystyle \frac{V(4,t+15)}{V(3,t)}=\displaystyle \frac{{@ageset_3b@}}{{@ageset_2a@}}={@p_3_rate@},    \text{p}_4=\displaystyle \frac{V(5,t+15)}{V(4,t)}=\displaystyle \frac{{@ageset_5b@}}{{@ageset_4a@}}={@p_4_rate@}\)</p>
<br>
<hr>
<p>To project the fertility rates from \(1957-1990\) we first have to determine the existing fertility rates for ages \(15-29\) and \(30-44\) in the years \(1960-1970\), we'll denote them as \(\text {f}_2\) and \(\text {f}_3\)</p>
<p> \(\begin{align}
\text {f}_2&=\displaystyle \frac{\text{live births for age (15-29)}}{\displaystyle \frac{V(2,t)+V(1,t)p_{1}15}{2}}\\
&=\displaystyle\frac{{@births_1@}}{({@ageset_2a@}+({@ageset_1a@} \times {@p_1_rate@})) \times (\displaystyle\frac{15}{2})}\\
&={@f_2@}\\
\end{align}\)</p>
<br>
<p> \(\begin{align}
\text {f}_3&=\displaystyle \frac{\text{live births for age (30-44)}}{\displaystyle\frac{V(3,t)+V(2,t)p_{1}15}{2}}\\
&=\displaystyle\frac{{@births_2@}}{({@ageset_3a@}+({@ageset_2a@} \times {@p_2_rate@})) \times (\displaystyle\frac{15}{2})}
&={@f_3@}\\
\end{align}\)</p>
<hr>
<p>So, the projected fertility rate \(f1,f2  \text{and}  f3\) will be</p>
<p>\(\text{f}1= \text{p}_1 \times \displaystyle \frac{15}{2} \times \text {f}_2 \times \textbf{p}_{b}\) </p>
<p>\(\quad ={@p_1_rate@} \times \displaystyle \frac{15}{2} \times {@p_b@}\)</p>
<p>\(\quad={@f1@} \)</p>

<p>\(\begin{align}
\text{f}2&= \text{p}_2 \times \displaystyle \frac{15}{2} \times \text {f}_3 \times \textbf{p}_{b} + \displaystyle \frac{15}{2} \times \text {f}_2 \times  \textbf{p}_{b}\\
&={@p_2_rate@} \times \displaystyle \frac{15}{2} \times  {@f_3@} \times {@p_b@} + \displaystyle \frac{15}{2} \times {@f_2@} \times {@p_b@}\\
&={@f2@} 
\end{align}\)</p>

<p>\(\begin{align}
\text{f}3 &= \displaystyle \frac{15}{2} \times \text {f}_3 \times \textbf{p}_{b} \\
&= \displaystyle \frac{15}{2} \times {@f_3@} \times {@p_b@}\\
&={@f3@} \\
\end{align}\)</p>
<br>
<hr>
<p>Therefore,</p>
<p>\(\begin{bmatrix}
{@f1@} &{@f2@}  & {@f3@} & 0 & 0\\ 
{@p_1_rate@} & 0 & 0 & 0 &0 \\ 
0 & {@p_2_rate@} & 0 &0  &0 \\ 
 0& 0 & {@p_3_rate@} & 0 & 0\\ 
0 & 0 &0  & {@p_4_rate@} & {@p_5_rate@}
\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}
v(1,t)\\ 
v(2,t)\\ 
v(3,t)\\ 
v(4,t)\\ 
v(5,t)
\end{bmatrix}\)</p>]]></text>
